.nh
.TH "AUTOSNAP" "1" "Jul 2026" "autosnap" "autosnap manual"

.SH NAME
autosnap-branch-create - Create and check out a Git branch with checkpoint refs


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBautosnap branch create  [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Create and check out a Git branch, then copy autosnap checkpoint refs
from the previously checked-out branch into the new branch namespace.

.PP
This is equivalent to git checkout -b  plus copying refs from
refs/autosnapshots// to refs/autosnapshots//.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for create

.PP
\fB--no-copy-checkpoints\fP[=false]
	Create the Git branch without copying checkpoint refs

.PP
\fB--overwrite\fP[=false]
	Replace colliding target checkpoint refs


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
autosnap branch create feature/next
autosnap branch create feature/next --no-copy-checkpoints
autosnap branch create feature/next --overwrite
.EE


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBautosnap-branch(1)\fP
